It is Saturday morning and I get up early.
I am helping at the café again today.
But first I have to take care of Bruno.
He cannot stay alone in the flat all morning.
We go outside for a short walk.
We walk once around the block.
Sabine has clear rules for him.
He must always stay on the lead.
He is not allowed to run around freely.
After ten minutes, we are back home.
Bruno immediately runs into the kitchen.
He whines quietly.
He is very hungry for his breakfast.
I open his dog food.
Bruno jumps up at me excitedly.
"No, Bruno," I say calmly.
"Sit!"
He looks at me and sits down.
"Good boy," I praise him.
Then I put his bowl on the floor.
